    "created_at": "2020-11-12T22:13:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-12T22:13:28Z",
    "body": "PR #1137 explicitly removed a clause that specified that the style block update algorithm should only work on \"element[s] whose node document has a browsing context\". Seems like this used to be explicit and was intentionally removed?\r\n\r\nI'm coming from discussion on [chromium#437153](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=437153), where the pre-1137 wording caused Chromium to have a misalignment with the spec ([see demo here](https://codesandbox.io/s/crbug437153-l5kpz?file=/index.html)).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
