    "created_at": "2020-11-12T22:20:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-12T22:20:29Z",
    "body": "Right, it was intentionally removed per @annevk's comments above, that `.sheet` exists for such cases.\r\n\r\nHowever, the test case you found (with XHR `responseDoc`s) is interesting, because Firefox gives it a null `.sheet` and Chrome gives it a `CSSStyleSheet` object. I guess `document.implementation.createHTMLDocument()` and XHR `responseDoc`s are treated differently by Firefox.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
