    "created_at": "2020-11-13T11:06:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-13T12:34:28Z",
    "body": "We should probably also test `DOMParser()` and `createContextualFragment()` (with various different documents) then.\r\n\r\nEdit: per @hsivonen Firefox has a \"data document\" concept that's used for `XMLHttpRequest` and `DOMParser`. I'm not sure if other browsers have that concept though and it doesn't seem great that `new Document()` wouldn't create that. Doing what OP suggests seems much more reasonable to me now, but I'm not sure how web compatible that is.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
